  {
    "_id": "a891053c3bbd9fc3",
    "name": "Artificing Materials",
    "pages": [
      {
        "_id": "0c9d41f616acddec",
        "name": "Artificing Materials",
        "type": "text",
        "title": {
          "show": true,
          "level": 1
        },
        "text": {
          "format": 1,
          "content": "<p>Artifice weapons follow special rules. Weapon attachments follow the regular artifice rules however.</p><p>Iron:<br>Equal artifice parts to the base clim cost of the artifice is required to craft Iron Artifices.</p><p>Outside of iron, there are a variety of special materials that an Artificer can use while crafting. These are more expensive, but grant additional C mod slots to the artifice.</p><p>You need Artifice Parts of the matching type to craft and the amount you need is determined this way:</p><p>(Special Material Modifier) x (Base Clim Cost) = Amount of Special Material Artifice Parts Needed</p><p>NOTE: When making an Artifice weapon that is an actual weapon and not an attachment, you must spend an additional iron artifice parts equal to the cost of the weapon - 500 rather than an extra ingot. This also applies to guns.</p><hr><p><small>Source: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1S7ygwpW8p6rqOjf7bfmfylhzx9R3uFfP3ZYBFGlDeLs/edit#gid=858813003\">Flo's Madness</a>. Prices ending in c are Clim; amounts ending in u are units.</small></p>"
        },
        "flags": {
          "lyrian-chronicles": {
            "seedKey": "flos-madness:crafting-guide--artificing-materials",
            "stableId": "crafting-guide--artificing-materials",
            "sourceUrl": "https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1S7ygwpW8p6rqOjf7bfmfylhzx9R3uFfP3ZYBFGlDeLs/edit#gid=858813003",
            "sourceHash": "b51bbab52015399e27611f94ca6b77f640d900144db7f5d5502c816a0e5eeb0e",
            "rulebookVersion": "Flo's Madness",
            "contentBuild": "0.6.0"
          }
        }
      }
    ],
